// `ctxc interp` (ctxc/eval.ctx) runs main in the interpreter over the IR, as `ctxc run` runs
// it compiled: arguments, a defer, a partial application, f32's printing, both streams and
// main's exit code.
//# $ ctxc interp {dir}/hello.ctx -- a "b c"
//# exit: 2
//# stdout:
//| b c
//| 42
//| 0.3
//| deferred
//# stderr:
//| to stderr
//# $ ctxc run {dir}/hello.ctx -- a "b c"
//# exit: 2
//# stdout:
//| b c
//| 42
//| 0.3
//| deferred
//# stderr:
//| to stderr
